(7167241, 1100754, 144365, '<td valign="top">Well done Art. <br/>Gave this a ten and hope to see it on the front page. Easily the best in the challenge.</td>', 'Well done Art. Gave this a ten and hope to see it on the front page. Easily the best in the challenge.', '2014-02-01 15:36:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(7167242, 1100719, 144365, '<td valign="top">It doesn''t fit what the inspiration for the challenge had in mind, but it''s too clever to not reward it with a decent vote. Giving this a nine.</td>', 'It doesn''t fit what the inspiration for the challenge had in mind, but it''s too clever to not reward it with a decent vote. Giving this a nine.', '2014-02-01 15:39:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(7167346, 1100626, 144365, '<td valign="top">Changing my comment a little. <br/> <br/>I voted this a one.<br/>The superimposition of your adult face being marred and hidden from your childhood hair adds no value. It obscures the vast majority of your face and makes it hard to see your expression. <br/> <br/>The description explicitly states: this week, go back in time and visit your childhood self, or perhaps have them warped into a future scene with you! The entries I was generous with attempted to insert themselves into a scene, which was the <a href="//www.mymodernmet.com/profiles/blogs/chino-otsuka-imagine-finding-me" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">inspiration</a> for this challenge. If there''s a scene present, I''m definitely missing it. <br/> <br/>Just wanted to add that yours isn''t the only image that I think missed the mark in this regard. It was just after seeing the thread you started, I had to comment. I think complaining about voters is detrimental to the overall site. People should be allowed to vote how they see fit without having people constantly complain about their voters. At least I''m trying to explain why I voted the way I did.</td>', 'Changing my comment a little.  I voted this a one.The superimposition of your adult face being marred and hidden from your childhood hair adds no value. It obscures the vast majority of your face and makes it hard to see your expression.  The description explicitly states: this week, go back in time and visit your childhood self, or perhaps have them warped into a future scene with you! The entries I was generous with attempted to insert themselves into a scene, which was the inspiration for this challenge. If there''s a scene present, I''m definitely missing it.  Just wanted to add that yours isn''t the only image that I think missed the mark in this regard. It was just after seeing the thread you started, I had to comment. I think complaining about voters is detrimental to the overall site. People should be allowed to vote how they see fit without having people constantly complain about their voters. At least I''m trying to explain why I voted the way I did.', '2014-02-01 17:31:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(7167415, 1100824, 42013, '<td valign="top">Awesome. Nice blend of time.</td>', 'Awesome. Nice blend of time.', '2014-02-01 19:26:31.000000', NULL, 1),
